{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed\r\nchange of use from House in Multiple Occupation (Class C4) to Childrens Home\r\n(Class C2)&amp;nbsp;would not fall within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 3 of\r\nthe&amp;nbsp;General Permitted Development Order (2015) (as amended).&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The change from a 7 person HMO (sui generis) to a 8 person HMO (sui generis) as proposed would materially alter the character of\r\nthe site’s usage, including a reduction in living conditions of future occupants\r\nassociated with the loss of communal space, and introduce additional external\r\npressures on bin storage, cycle storage, the local transport network and greater noise and disturbance\r\ngenerated by occupants, and therefore be development requiring full planning\r\npermission. As there is no such extant permission, the development is\r\nconsidered unlawful&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
